  "summary": "The verification-results.json is an internally consistent, honest terminal-state verification ledger. The headline tally (118 required checks = 92 scenarios + 26 infra/journey checks; 104 PASS / 9 known environment drift / 3 UNVERIFIED / 2 FAIL) reconciles exactly with a per-row recount, and every non-PASS disposition carries a note, evidence path, and (except one gap) a named holder. The three real journeys are documented with concrete real-world identifiers (real SIGKILL windows pre/post-commit with rollback/roll-forward verification, real Outline revocation->isolation->restore on the Run's own published documentId with 24s detection), the seven P1 bindings each provide fix commits, counterexample-green evidence, and a final readback at the recorded baseline, and goal_complete=false is stated with a specific, non-inflated reason. Residual weaknesses are minor and non-blocking: recorded exit codes disagree with PASS status in four rows (explained only in notes), V_FULL_CHECK's fixture gap lacks a findings/ledger entry with a holder, the 9-check drift cohort rests on an exact-match signature rather than a green pinned-environment run, and the artifact does not itself tie baseline 6918798 to the delivered-artifact commit 0dcfec1. None of these undermine the gated decision, which is to accept the VERIFY node and the run's completion as honestly reported evidence — not to claim the overall goal complete — so APPROVE is warranted.",
